<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince Frederick of Noer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1800">1800</a>–<a href="/years/1865">1865</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Frederick of Schleswig-Holstein-Sonderburg-Augustenburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince Frederick of Noer, of the Augustenburg branch of the Danish royal house, was a leader of the German movement in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a>. In March 1848 he joined the provisional government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiel">Kiel</a> and took command of its army, seizing the fortress of Rendsburg at the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-schleswig-war">First Schleswig War</a>. He later went into exile and lived on his estate of Noer.</p></div>
